1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:31,570 --> 00:01:35,620
It seems you've refused to allow
the interrogation of the pilot of Unit 01,

37
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:39,630
the only one directly involved
in the incident, Major Katsuragi.

38
00:01:39,630 --> 00:01:42,860
Yes, Sir. He is very unstable,
emotionally speaking.

39
00:01:42,860 --> 00:01:45,370
I believe that it would be
unwise to have him here.

40
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:49,070
Then, as his proxy, let us ask you,
Major Katsuragi.

41
00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:50,470
In this incident,

42
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:55,080
did the Angel not attempt to
communicate with us, mankind?

43
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:57,810
I find no suggestion of that
in the subject's report.

44
00:01:57,810 --> 00:02:00,250
It is believed to have been an irregular incident.

45
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,820
Assuming his memory is correct.

46
00:02:02,820 --> 00:02:05,490
There is no evidence that his memory
has been tampered with.

47
00:02:05,490 --> 00:02:08,590
However, the Eva's AC recorder
was not functioning.

48
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:09,890
There's no way to confirm it.

49
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:13,660
Was the Angel interested in the human psyche?
In the human mind?

50
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:15,660
I am unable to answer that question.

51
00:02:15,660 --> 00:02:18,600
Whether the Angels even have
a concept of what a mind is,

52
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,000
or whether they can understand
human thoughts or not,

53
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,440
is completely unknown.

54
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:28,040
This incident has a new element in it,
in that the Angel tried to take an Eva into itself.

55
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,780
Is there any possibility that this

56
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:33,650
may be linked to the predicted Thirteenth Angel
and all Angels thereafter?

57
00:02:33,650 --> 00:02:35,120
Based on the pattern thus far,

58
00:02:35,120 --> 00:02:38,190
there is nothing to suggest such a systematic
organization among the Angels.

59
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:43,160
Correct! It is obvious that they have
worked independently, so far.

60
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:45,030
What do you mean, Sir?

61
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:47,060
You are not allowed to ask questions.

62
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:47,560
Yes, Sir.

63
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,460
That will be all. Dismissed.

64
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:51,050
Yes, Sir.

65
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:55,670
What do you think, Ikari?

66
00:02:55,670 --> 00:02:58,410
The Angels are beginning to attain intelligence.

67
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:59,740
The time left to us is...

68
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:02,660
EPISODE 17
THE FOURTH
QUALIFIED
INDIVIDUAL

69
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:02,660
Running short?

70
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,550
The patient in Room 12?

71
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:09,680
The emergency room patient
from that E incident, right?

72
00:03:09,680 --> 00:03:11,920
She's been hospitalized here for a long time.

73
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:14,590
I've heard her injuries are really complicated.

74
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:16,460
She's still in elementary school.

75
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:18,230
He's here again today, right?

76
00:03:18,230 --> 00:03:22,200
Yeah, he comes to see her
at least twice a week.

77
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,630
He's a good and caring brother.

78
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:29,890
Suzuhara

79
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:29,890
Empty

80
00:03:24,390 --> 00:03:29,890
Empty

81
00:03:24,630 --> 00:03:28,890
Yeah, boys like that are pretty rare these days.

82
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:34,510
Rei, are you all right today?

83
00:03:34,510 --> 00:03:38,180
Yes, Sir. I will go see Dr. Akagi tomorrow,

84
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:40,420
and the day after I'll be at school.

85
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,880
How is school?

86
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,020
No problems, Sir.

87
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,870
I see. That's good.

88
00:03:46,300 --> 00:03:49,410
Stand! Bow! Sit down!

89
00:03:51,510 --> 00:03:54,460
Today's absences are the usual Ayanami,
and Aida?

90
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,200
What's up with Kensuke?

91
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,700
Mr. Koike is also absent today,

92
00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:01,200
New Yokosuka. Chasin' battleships again today.

93
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,970
So the class in modern Japanese
will be self-study.

94
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:04,140
A ship called Myoko, or somethin'
like that, is in port.

95
00:04:01,970 --> 00:04:04,140
And finally, the student
on duty today will be...

96
00:04:04,140 --> 00:04:05,070
Suzuhara.

97
00:04:05,070 --> 00:04:06,810
Yes, Sir!

98
00:04:06,810 --> 00:04:09,740
Deliver the printouts to Ayanami after school.

99
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:10,270
Yes, Sir!

100
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:16,380
Anyway, 1st Branch is okay, right?

101
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,420
Send the info from Satellite 5 immediately.
It's top priority.

102
00:04:15,030 --> 00:04:17,420
Just the schedule for Unit 04 is fine.

103
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:20,400
It doesn't matter, we'll have the Magi evaluate
the data discrepancies from the sensors!

104
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,400
I'd like confirmation on the synchro data
and the S2 engine.

105
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,400
We'll get rid of the noise over on our end.
Just send us the originals.

106
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:22,620
It vanished?!

107
00:04:22,620 --> 00:04:25,360
You're sure the 2nd Branch just vanished?!

108
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:27,430
Yes, Sir, it's been confirmed.

109
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:28,700
It vanished.

110
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:31,300
Oh, man...

111
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,870
The Administration and Investigation
departments are going crazy,

112
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:35,800
and General Affairs is in a total panic.

113
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,880
So what was the cause?

114
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,470
We still don't know.

115
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:41,240
Our only clues are these
geosynchronous satellite photos.

116
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:43,420
There's nothing else left.

117
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,030
10 seconds...

118
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:48,620
8...

119
00:04:48,620 --> 00:04:49,550
7...

120
00:04:49,550 --> 00:04:50,520
6...

121
00:04:50,520 --> 00:04:51,420
5...

122
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:52,350
4...

123
00:04:52,350 --> 00:04:53,190
3...

124
00:04:53,190 --> 00:04:54,060
2...

125
00:04:54,060 --> 00:04:54,940
1...

126
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:56,480
Contact.

127
00:05:05,210 --> 00:05:06,670
This is horrible.

128
00:05:06,670 --> 00:05:11,670
Evangelion Unit 04 and all related
research facilities within an 89km radius

129
00:05:11,670 --> 00:05:13,210
have completely vanished.

130
00:05:13,210 --> 00:05:15,680
Along with several thousand people.

131
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:19,010
Looking at the time schedule,
we believe it to be an accident

132
00:05:19,010 --> 00:05:22,220
during the experimental installation of
the S2 engine that was restored in Germany.

133
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:23,520
Potential causes range from

134
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:26,490
a lack of structural integrity to
a preliminary design stage error.

135
00:05:26,490 --> 00:05:29,220
That's 32,768 possibilities right there.

136
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:31,330
And there's also the chance of sabotage.

137
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:36,000
But it didn't explode, it vanished, right?
In other words, it disappeared.

138
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,230
In all probability, they were swallowed
by a Sea of Dirac,

139
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:40,870
just like Unit 01 was.

140
00:05:40,870 --> 00:05:43,140
And the S2 engine that we finally restored?

141
00:05:43,140 --> 00:05:45,510
Gone. Our dream's been shattered.

142
00:05:45,510 --> 00:05:48,510
That's what we get for trying to push ourselves
into using something we don't understand.

143
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:50,450
That goes for the Evas too.

144
00:05:51,930 --> 00:05:54,580
So, what about the remaining Unit 03?

145
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,750
We're going to base it here.

146
00:05:56,750 --> 00:06:00,090
It seems the U.S. Government doesn't
want to lose the 1st Branch as well.

147
00:06:00,090 --> 00:06:05,090
They're the ones who insisted on
the right to build Units 03 and 04.

148
00:06:05,090 --> 00:06:07,760
And now they're foisting just
the dangerous parts off on us?

149
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:09,400
Talk about self-serving bastards.

150
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:13,000
After a disaster like that,
anyone would get nervous.

151
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:15,140
So what are you going to do
about the activation test?

152
00:06:15,140 --> 00:06:17,320
Will you use that dummy plug?

153
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,520
I've still got to decide that.

154
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:23,380
This is the dummy plug prototype.

155
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,650
Rei's personal data has been loaded into it,

156
00:06:25,650 --> 00:06:29,650
but it's not really possible to digitize
a human mind and soul.

157
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:32,420
Ultimately, it's a fake, an imitation.

158
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:36,160
Just a machine that emulates
a pilot's thinking process.

159
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:38,890
It'll transmit a signal pattern to the Eva.

160
00:06:38,890 --> 00:06:43,400
As long as the Eva believes there's a pilot
and synchronizes, that's enough.

161
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,270
Load the data into Unit 01 and Unit 02.

162
00:06:46,270 --> 00:06:48,400
There are still some problems with it.

163
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,070
That's not important. As long as
the Eva activates, it's sufficient.

164
00:06:51,070 --> 00:06:51,260
Yes, Sir.

165
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:57,750
I've delegated the transportation
of the Unit to the U.N.

166
00:06:57,750 --> 00:07:00,050
It should arrive by the end of the week.

167
00:07:00,050 --> 00:07:02,120
You take care of the rest.

168
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,180
Yes, Sir.

169
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:06,650
We'll perform the modifications
and activation test in Matsushiro.

170
00:07:06,650 --> 00:07:08,060
What about the test pilot?

171
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,060
The dummy plug is still risky.

172
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,760
Of our prospective candidates...

173
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,530
We'll select a fourth, then?

174
00:07:13,530 --> 00:07:18,200
Yes, there is one child whose core
can be prepared immediately.

175
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,300
Then I'll leave it to you.

176
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,890
Yes, Sir.

177
00:07:21,550 --> 00:07:23,760
Rei, you can come out now.

178
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:25,510
Yes, Sir.

179
00:07:25,510 --> 00:07:26,940
Let's eat.

180
00:07:26,940 --> 00:07:27,960
Yes, Sir.

181
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:37,310
Stand! Bow!

182
00:07:37,970 --> 00:07:42,590
Lunch time! Lunch time! This is the
single best thing 'bout school.

183
00:07:42,590 --> 00:07:44,510
What?!

184
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:48,060
You didn't bring lunch?

185
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:51,170
I didn't have time to cook last night
because of homework.

186
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:55,310
And so you're telling me to go without lunch?!

187
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,910
What's this? Married couple fightin' again?

188
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,580
It's not like that!

189
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:06,540
What's all this formality for?

190
00:08:07,830 --> 00:08:10,650
It's the Unit 03 activation test at Matsushiro.

191
00:08:10,650 --> 00:08:13,090
We'll be using the fourth as the pilot.

192
00:08:13,090 --> 00:08:14,290
The fourth?

193
00:08:14,290 --> 00:08:16,860
The Fourth Child's been found?

194
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:18,360
Just yesterday.

195
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:21,460
But I haven't received a report
from the Marduk Institute.

196
00:08:21,460 --> 00:08:23,440
The official documents will be
delivered tomorrow.

197
00:08:26,650 --> 00:08:30,710
Dr. Akagi, aren't you hiding
something from me again?

198
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:32,170
Not really.

199
00:08:32,170 --> 00:08:35,630
Well, okay. So, who's the selected kid?

200
00:08:41,330 --> 00:08:43,990
Of all the people, it's that child?

201
00:08:43,990 --> 00:08:45,420
It can't be helped.

202
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:47,960
All the candidates were gathered
together for protection.

203
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:50,530
It'll be hard to break to them.

204
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:54,330
Asuka will be fine. Her pride's
riding on her piloting of the Eva.

205
00:08:54,330 --> 00:08:56,730
And Rei is an exception,

206
00:08:56,730 --> 00:09:00,540
but nothing good comes of becoming
involved with us and the Evas.

207
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:04,270
Shinji understands that better than anybody.

208
00:09:04,270 --> 00:09:07,220
I don't want him to suffer any more hardships.

209
00:09:07,220 --> 00:09:10,520
But we need children of this kind,

210
00:09:11,290 --> 00:09:13,920
in order for us all to survive.

211
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:16,200
Let go of the pure ideals,
is that what you're saying?

212
00:09:24,770 --> 00:09:28,630
Suzuhara, you're on duty this week,
so get to it!

213
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:29,700
What do you mean?

214
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:31,530
The printout!

215
00:09:30,380 --> 00:09:31,460
Emergency Evacuation Training
Enforcement Notice

216
00:09:31,530 --> 00:09:34,100
Didn't our teacher tell you to deliver this?

217
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:37,210
C'mon, class rep, you can ask
the other person on duty.

218
00:09:37,210 --> 00:09:39,340
Miss Ayanami is absent today!

219
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:41,380
It's Ayanami and me?

220
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,120
Can't be helped then.

221
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:46,680
But I can't exactly go to a girl's place alone.

222
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,320
Well, in that case, I'll go along...

223
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:50,120
Shinji!

224
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,060
Walk home with me, will ya?

225
00:10:14,990 --> 00:10:17,910
Ayanami, we're coming in.

226
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:21,050
I don't think it's good to barge into
a girl's room without her permission.

227
00:10:21,050 --> 00:10:22,350
We've got no choice.

228
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:23,890
She won't see it if we leave it there.

229
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:28,770
Excuse us...

230
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:39,830
Wha?!

231
00:10:39,830 --> 00:10:43,620
Is this a girl's room? It's so unwelcomin'.

232
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:52,920
Notice
Class News

233
00:10:59,730 --> 00:11:02,720
Hey, you shouldn't touch anythin'!
She'll get pissed!

234
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,810
I'm just cleaning up.

235
00:11:05,570 --> 00:11:07,800
I ain't helpin'!

236
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,500
That's not a man's job!

237
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,950
Okay, but Miss Misato hates guys like that.

238
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:17,360
I don't care! It's my policy!

239
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:25,260
Man, what a change.

240
00:11:25,930 --> 00:11:27,050
In what?

241
00:11:27,050 --> 00:11:27,910
You.

242
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:35,300
The first time I saw you,
I really thought you were a jerk.

243
00:11:35,770 --> 00:11:38,880
And you didn't seem like you'd
do somethin' for others.

244
00:11:40,210 --> 00:11:43,880
Well, I guess it depends on
what you've got to give.

245
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:54,840
We're visitin'!

246
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,840
What?

247
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,440
Those are the printouts that were pilin' up.

248
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,450
I'm sorry.

249
00:12:04,450 --> 00:12:07,240
I took it upon myself to clean up a little.
But I didn't touch anything except trash.

250
00:12:10,370 --> 00:12:12,410
Thank you.

251
00:12:16,810 --> 00:12:21,630
Eva pilots sure are weird, all right.

252
00:12:29,820 --> 00:12:31,530
Thank you...

253
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:34,420
Words of gratitude.

254
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:35,690
Words I've never used.

255
00:12:38,870 --> 00:12:41,230
I'd never even said them to him.

256
00:12:48,610 --> 00:12:52,660
The city, a paradise made by mankind.

257
00:12:53,250 --> 00:12:55,600
Once driven from Paradise,

258
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:59,720
man had no choice but to escape to this
earthly existence, side by side with death.

259
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:02,110
Our own paradise,

260
00:13:02,110 --> 00:13:06,950
created by the resourcefulness that this
weakest of beings was forced to develop.

261
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:09,550
To protect ourselves from the fear of death,

262
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:12,320
to satiate our thirst for pleasure,

263
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:15,140
a paradise we created ourselves.

264
00:13:15,970 --> 00:13:21,060
This city's truly such a paradise.
A armed city made to protect us.

265
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:25,710
A city of cowards fleeing from
the outside world, filled with enemies.

266
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:32,070
Cowards do live longer. That's fine.

267
00:13:32,070 --> 00:13:36,340
New Tokyo-3, Nerv's camouflaged
intercept fortress.

268
00:13:36,340 --> 00:13:40,050
The continually-delayed seventh
construction phase will be finished soon.

269
00:13:40,050 --> 00:13:42,420
At long last, it will be completed.

270
00:13:46,170 --> 00:13:50,970
How will you report Unit 04's accident
to the Committee?

271
00:13:50,970 --> 00:13:53,930
Just as the facts state, the cause is unknown.

272
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:58,070
But at this stage, it's a catastrophic loss.

273
00:13:58,070 --> 00:14:00,300
Unit 04 and the 2nd Branch are acceptable.

274
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:02,840
Even with the S2 engine,
we may have lost the sample,

275
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:05,470
but we still have the data in Germany.

276
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:08,380
This installation and Unit 01 will be sufficient.

277
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:11,160
But the Committee was furious.

278
00:14:11,630 --> 00:14:14,260
Of course, it was an unscheduled accident.

279
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:17,710
Seele must also be frantically
adjusting the schedule.

280
00:14:18,430 --> 00:14:21,120
Incidents not depicted in the
Dead Sea Scrolls can occur.

281
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:23,600
This ought to teach the old men a lesson.

282
00:14:28,230 --> 00:14:31,130
The intercept system here is finally
going to be completed,

283
00:14:31,130 --> 00:14:33,970
and there isn't even one measly party planned?

284
00:14:33,970 --> 00:14:36,000
Nerv sure is an uptight organization.

285
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,890
Well, you know how Commander Ikari is.

286
00:14:38,550 --> 00:14:40,230
What about you?

287
00:14:40,690 --> 00:14:42,710
Are you serious, Mr. Kaji?

288
00:14:42,710 --> 00:14:45,750
I'll tell Miss Katsuragi and Dr. Akagi.

289
00:14:45,750 --> 00:14:47,850
I'll cover up your mouth first...

290
00:14:47,850 --> 00:14:49,580
So how's work going?

291
00:14:49,580 --> 00:14:51,590
Oh, it's going, I guess.

292
00:14:51,590 --> 00:14:54,400
Well, I have work to do. Excuse me.

293
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:58,800
Far be it from me to comment
on your private life,

294
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:03,460
but would you keep your hands off
our young girls in this emergency situation?

295
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:05,730
This isn't your jurisdiction, though, is it?

296
00:15:05,730 --> 00:15:07,500
Could I hit on you then?

297
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,300
That depends on how you answer my questions.

298
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:12,430
You know the secrets of Adam down there
and the Marduk Institute, right?

299
00:15:13,510 --> 00:15:14,680
What secrets?

300
00:15:14,680 --> 00:15:16,240
Don't play dumb!

301
00:15:16,240 --> 00:15:18,780
Asking for help isn't like you.

302
00:15:18,780 --> 00:15:22,350
I can't afford to care right now.
I don't have that luxury.

303
00:15:22,350 --> 00:15:26,350
What's behind the oh-so-convenient
discovery of the Fourth Child?

304
00:15:26,350 --> 00:15:28,910
I'll tell you one thing.

305
00:15:30,470 --> 00:15:32,460
The Marduk Institute doesn't exist.

306
00:15:32,460 --> 00:15:35,130
Nerv itself is pulling the strings.

307
00:15:35,130 --> 00:15:36,930
Nerv itself?

308
00:15:36,930 --> 00:15:37,830
Commander Ikari?

309
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:40,300
Go check out Code 707.

310
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:41,890
707?

311
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,440
Shinji's school?

312
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:46,170
Miss Misato!

313
00:15:46,170 --> 00:15:46,970
What is it?

314
00:15:46,970 --> 00:15:50,110
Miss Ritsuko wants to see you about
the business trip you're going on tomorrow.

315
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:51,010
All right. Thank you.

316
00:15:52,090 --> 00:15:53,310
I'll catch you later.

317
00:15:53,310 --> 00:15:54,140
Yes, Ma'am.

318
00:15:58,030 --> 00:16:00,690
How about it? Wanna go out for tea?

319
00:16:00,690 --> 00:16:02,100
You know, I'm a boy.

320
00:16:06,900 --> 00:16:10,840
I thought you'd be a more
serious person, Mr. Kaji.

321
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:14,500
Once you're comfortable around someone,
you sure don't hold back, Shinji Ikari.

322
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,800
I'm sorry.

323
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:20,450
No, I'm sorry too. I didn't mean
to sound sarcastic.

324
00:16:21,890 --> 00:16:25,260
I know! I'll show you something neat.

325
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:30,180
Are they watermelons?

326
00:16:30,180 --> 00:16:33,070
Yeah, aren't they cute? This is my hobby.

327
00:16:33,670 --> 00:16:34,970
It's a secret from everybody else, though.

328
00:16:36,040 --> 00:16:39,160
Making something...
Nurturing something is really great.

329
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:40,850
You can see and learn so many things
from the process.

330
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:43,830
Like what's enjoyable.

331
00:16:43,830 --> 00:16:45,420
And about suffering too, right?

332
00:16:48,480 --> 00:16:50,190
Do you hate suffering?

333
00:16:50,750 --> 00:16:52,440
I don't like it.

334
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,700
Have you found anything that you enjoy?

335
00:16:57,260 --> 00:16:58,750
That's fine too.

336
00:16:58,750 --> 00:17:03,380
But knowledge of suffering makes you
all the more capable of kindness to others.

337
00:17:03,380 --> 00:17:05,370
Because that's different from being weak.

338
00:17:06,770 --> 00:17:08,470
Yes? Hello?

339
00:17:10,870 --> 00:17:12,460
It's Katsuragi.

340
00:17:12,460 --> 00:17:14,420
She says they're starting the synch test.

341
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:17,340
<i>Fix the depth at 3.2.</i>

342
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:20,530
I thought so. Shinji's synch rate is dropping.

343
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:19,470
<i>LCL thickness is nominal.</i>

344
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:22,640
<i>Harmonics level is negative 1.1...</i>

345
00:17:20,530 --> 00:17:21,940
What's that mean?

346
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:23,500
I can't say.

347
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:23,670
<i>0.5...</i>

348
00:17:23,500 --> 00:17:26,840
But something must have happened
during that incident.

349
00:17:23,670 --> 00:17:24,970
<i>0.9...</i>

350
00:17:24,970 --> 00:17:27,680
<i>0.10...</i>

351
00:17:26,840 --> 00:17:28,710
Something psychological.

352
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:30,010
<i>Current exponent is 0.9.</i>

353
00:17:28,710 --> 00:17:31,880
This makes it even harder to tell him
about Unit 03's pilot.

354
00:17:30,010 --> 00:17:33,900
<i>All results posted to Melchior.</i>

355
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:35,110
But the pilot will be officially informed tomorrow.

356
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:41,610
Stand! Attention! Bow!

357
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:44,760
Lunch time!

358
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:44,760
<i><i>Toji Suzuhara of Class 2-A.</i></i>

359
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:47,500
<i><i>Toji Suzuhara, report to the Principal's Office.</i></i>

360
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:48,960
What the...

361
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,550
Did you do something?

362
00:17:51,250 --> 00:17:53,750
No, nothin' comes to mind.

363
00:17:54,130 --> 00:18:02,180
Principal's Office

364
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:58,460
Excuse me, I'm Toji Suzuhara.

365
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,140
You're Toji Suzuhara?

366
00:18:04,690 --> 00:18:07,010
How was your trip to New Yokosuka yesterday?

367
00:18:07,010 --> 00:18:08,380
Way cool!

368
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:11,560
Speaking of which, I picked up
some interesting information.

369
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:14,890
Eva Unit 03?

370
00:18:14,890 --> 00:18:18,930
Yeah, the one they were building in America.
It's completed, isn't it?

371
00:18:18,930 --> 00:18:20,390
I don't know.

372
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:24,030
I know you've got to keep it a secret,
but please tell me.

373
00:18:24,030 --> 00:18:25,900
I really haven't heard anything!

374
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:27,770
Haven't you heard the rumor
that the activation test

375
00:18:27,770 --> 00:18:30,240
will be held at the second test facility
in Matsushiro?

376
00:18:30,240 --> 00:18:31,270
I haven't.

377
00:18:31,270 --> 00:18:33,210
The pilot hasn't been chosen yet, right?

378
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:35,060
I don't know about that stuff.

379
00:18:35,460 --> 00:18:38,980
I wish Miss Misato would pick me for it.

380
00:18:38,980 --> 00:18:42,780
Hey, Shinji, would you ask her for me too?
I want to be an Eva pilot!

381
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:44,140
Really, I don't know.

382
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:49,960
Then what about the story
that Unit 04's been lost?

383
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:50,990
What was that?

384
00:18:50,990 --> 00:18:52,770
You really don't know about that either?

385
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,900
It disappeared along with the entire 2nd Branch.

386
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:58,300
I heard my dad's section was in a panic.

387
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,430
Really?

388
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:00,940
Probably.

389
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:02,780
I haven't heard anything from Miss Misato.

390
00:19:04,590 --> 00:19:08,080
Well, I guess it doesn't concern
pilots out on the line.

391
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:11,710
If she didn't tell you, it's likely because
you don't need to know.

392
00:19:13,130 --> 00:19:16,100
Sorry about bothering you with weird questions.

393
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:20,560
But Toji sure is taking a long time.

394
00:19:20,970 --> 00:19:22,660
Thus, we, mankind,

395
00:19:22,660 --> 00:19:27,600
survived the hell on Earth called
the Second Impact and rose again.

396
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:30,100
The number of children has
been decreasing yearly...

397
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:32,200
Sorry I'm late.

398
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:34,870
I've already heard. Take your seat.

399
00:19:34,870 --> 00:19:38,320
Anyway, it is you, the younger generation,
who will lead the way to the future...

400
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:43,780
Come on, let's go home.

401
00:19:43,780 --> 00:19:44,710
What about Toji?

402
00:19:44,710 --> 00:19:46,810
He'll be late.

403
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:48,450
He's got class duty.

404
00:19:58,410 --> 00:20:00,090
The school is now closing.

405
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:03,420
All students must go home immediately.

406
00:20:01,710 --> 00:20:03,420
Suzuhara!

407
00:20:04,150 --> 00:20:06,950
You're on duty,

408
00:20:07,550 --> 00:20:10,600
so make sure you line up the desks
and write up the daily record.

409
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:14,780
I haven't had lunch yet.
I'll do it as soon as I've eaten.

410
00:20:14,780 --> 00:20:17,650
Suzuhara, you always buy your lunch
from the school co-op.

411
00:20:17,650 --> 00:20:19,360
It's not like I've got anyone to cook for me.

412
00:20:22,660 --> 00:20:24,110
Suzuhara...

413
00:20:24,110 --> 00:20:24,860
Milk

414
00:20:25,730 --> 00:20:30,060
I have two sisters, named Kodama and Nozomi.

415
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:32,610
I always cook lunch for them, but...

416
00:20:32,910 --> 00:20:34,830
Must be a lot of work.

417
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:39,030
So, I'm actually a good cook,
though you might not think it.

418
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:40,530
Really?

419
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:44,450
And I always end up cooking
too much for our lunches.

420
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:47,050
What a waste.

421
00:20:47,460 --> 00:20:50,340
If you need help gettin' rid
of your leftovers, I'll help.

422
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:52,890
Yes, help me.

423
00:20:52,890 --> 00:21:00,690
District 3 transformation test complete.

424
00:21:00,690 --> 00:21:01,660
Mr. Kaji?

425
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:05,070
Oh, Asuka? Sorry, I'm a little busy
right now. Later, okay?

426
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:09,180
But you make time for Misato.

427
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:15,480
Hey, not right now!

428
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:18,590
These are our synch data reports, right?

429
00:21:19,050 --> 00:21:20,670
Four of them?

430
00:21:20,670 --> 00:21:23,360
What in the hell is this? What's going on?

431
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:25,910
Why is HE the Fourth Child?

432
00:21:25,910 --> 00:21:28,890
No! I don't understand! What is this?!

433
00:21:28,930 --> 00:21:31,640
NERV 1st BRANCH, USA

434
00:21:57,920 --> 00:22:00,710
TO BE CONTINUED

435
00:23:06,230 --> 00:23:07,240
PREVIEW

436
00:23:07,190 --> 00:23:12,290
Eva Unit 03 is delivered to Matsushiro
from America for the activation test.

437
00:23:12,290 --> 00:23:17,400
Unaware of the coming tragedy,
people gloried in the last of their daily lives.

438
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:20,010
Next episode: "The Selection of Life"

439
00:23:19,080 --> 00:23:21,250
THE SELECTION OF LIFE
